

<ps> displays info about running processes

<ps aux> displays all processes running in the system

<ps aux | grep apache2> Displays all services, and sends the output to grep, which will look through the output for the keyword "apache2"
  - Then displays only relevant output









find

<find / -type f -name apache2>
Find command, starting at the top of the directory, goes through every directory looking for "apache2" in the filename, and then lists everything found.

< find /etc -type f -name apache2>

  - Specify the directory with "/etc", searches only that directory and its subdirectories

.\* will allow you to search without knowing the file extension name
